# Dependencies (none currently, but future-proof for tooling)
node_modules/

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# Editor/IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
reference/

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Env/secrets
# .env.local holds the local build keys (POKEWALLET_IO_PROD_KEY, APITCG_KEY) — see
# README "Build keys". CI supplies keys as repo secrets instead, so they are never
# committed either way. The wildcard covers .env.production and friends too.
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem

# Probe output holds the probed service's card data (PokéWallet's terms grant no right
# to republish it) — keep it local (tools/*-probe.mjs, tools/jp-gap-size.mjs).
tools/apitcg-probe-report.md
tools/pokewallet-probe-report.md
tools/pokewallet-probe-images/
tools/jp-gap-size-report.md
tools/jp-gap-size.json

# Hosted card images (tools/build-images.mjs). LOCAL ONLY until PokéWallet agrees to us
# republishing them: committing either path publishes the files on GitHub Pages. To go
# live, delete these two lines and add the build step to refresh-data.yml (README,
# "Hosted card images").
img/
data/img-index.json
# Japanese card catalogue (tools/build-jp-catalog.mjs). data/jp-cat/ — set names, card
# numbers and card names — IS committed: the app serves it. Everything below stays local:
# the build-side copy carries PokéWallet's own card ids, and the raw per-set cache is
# their full API answers. To withdraw the published list, revert the commit that added
# data/jp-cat/; the app falls back to Bulbapedia on its own when the files are gone.
data/jp-catalog/
tools/jp-catalog-report.md
tools/.cache/

# Claude Code tooling (local-only, not shared with the team)
.claude

# Dev/session scratch notes, not project documentation
PROGRESS.md